xnu 0411: put the interface back on the carve-out before a reset

A `reboot` from the direct-scanout path leaves the bootloader's fastboot
with no USB at all: SRC0 still names an IOVA and context bank 3 still
translates it, and ABL does not recover the port from that -- measured on
every reset from an `mfs` boot, while the copy path resets cleanly. 0409's
port power-down alone was not enough.

So the reset path calls the framebuffer before the gadget: SRC0 goes back to
the physical carve-out and the bank's SCTLR is cleared, then the USB port is
powered down (0409) and the SoC resets.

--- a/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c
@@ -1661,9 +1661,17 @@ void
 mondrian_reboot_to_fastboot(void)
 {
 	extern void mondrian_usb_stop(void);
+	extern void mondrian_fb_shutdown(void);
 
 	mondrian_sync_before_reset("the reset to fastboot");
 	mondrian_log_flush_now();
+	/*
+	 * The interface must not still be fetching from an IOVA when the SoC
+	 * goes down: a warm reset from the direct-scanout path leaves the
+	 * bootloader with no USB at all, while the copy path resets cleanly.
+	 * Put SRC0 back on the carve-out and leave the bank bypassing first.
+	 */
+	mondrian_fb_shutdown();
 	/* The gadget must be idle before the SoC reset (0307). */
 	mondrian_usb_stop();
